WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
On a lab track, a one kilogram trolley
with a pin rolls at four metres per second.

2
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.200
Ahead, a three kilogram
trolley sits still,

3
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.560
a cork pad facing the pin.

4
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.380
Thud.

5
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:15.960
The pin sinks in, and the
two roll off together.

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.480
So how fast does the joined pair move?

7
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.580
Still four metres per second, or slower?

8
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:26.130
In this mission, you'll meet
momentum: mass times velocity.

9
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.920
It's a vector, so direction matters.

10
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.590
You'll see that, with no external impulse,

11
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.670
total momentum before
equals total momentum after.

12
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.700
And that when bodies coalesce,
they stick and share one velocity.

13
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: work out how fast
the trolleys move once they stick.
